# A single .jar file can contain multiple plugins, specified in separate lines.
#
# The format is: <menu>, "<menu label>", <class name>
#
# If something like ("<arg>") is appended to the class name, the setup() method
# will get that as arg parameter; otherwise arg is simply the empty string.

Plugins>TERRAPINS, "Workflow", com.coxphysics.terrapins.plugins.TERRAPINS.TERRAPINSPlugin
Plugins>TERRAPINS, "Results Viewer", com.coxphysics.terrapins.plugins.assessment.results.Plugin
Plugins>TERRAPINS, "HAWK Stream", com.coxphysics.terrapins.plugins.hawk.HAWKPlugin

# The fast moment fitter, kept reachable on its own. Localising without running a
# full assessment is a reasonable thing to want. Its sources are vendored into
# this module (see imagej/PROVENANCE.md), so these entries belong here rather
# than arriving from a dependency's own plugins.config.
Plugins>Fast SMLM, "Fast moment fitting", smlm.fastfit.FastFitterPlugIn("simple")
Plugins>Fast SMLM, "Fast moment fitting (advanced)...", smlm.fastfit.FastFitterPlugIn("advanced")

# The vendored ThunderSTORM (imagej/PROVENANCE.md). Registered under names of our
# own, not its usual ones, for two reasons: a user may well have ThunderSTORM
# installed already and two plugins claiming "Run analysis" would leave which one
# runs down to jar ordering; and these are how the one-click path reaches this
# copy specifically rather than whichever ImageJ happened to register.
#
# Only what the one-click path drives is registered. The rest of ThunderSTORM's
# menu - visualisation, calibration, simulation, colocalisation - is not exposed
# here, so a user who wants the whole application still installs it separately and
# gets it unshadowed by this one.
# Listed last and NOT as a submenu. ImageJ places a submenu above the plain items
# of its parent whatever order they appear in here, which put ThunderSTORM above
# Workflow - and Workflow is what someone opening this menu came for. As plain
# entries the file order is the menu order, so these sit at the bottom.
#
# They exist so IJ.run can reach this copy; they are plumbing rather than
# features, and the separator above them says so as clearly as a menu can.
Plugins>TERRAPINS, "-", -
Plugins>TERRAPINS, "Camera setup (TERRAPINS)", com.coxphysics.terrapins.vendored.thunderstorm.CameraSetupPlugIn
Plugins>TERRAPINS, "Run analysis (TERRAPINS)", com.coxphysics.terrapins.vendored.thunderstorm.AnalysisPlugIn("runAnalysis")
Plugins>TERRAPINS, "Show results table (TERRAPINS)", com.coxphysics.terrapins.vendored.thunderstorm.results.TableHandlerPlugin
Plugins>TERRAPINS, "Export results (TERRAPINS)", com.coxphysics.terrapins.vendored.thunderstorm.ImportExportPlugIn("export;results")
